Z||000006||Formula88||07-28-2001||01:06 PM||||Hey, might as well give it a shot.  It all depends on driver skill.  The VTEC doesn't kick in until high rpm's, and some drivers don't like revving their engines very high.  You run into an S2000 owner who shifts at 5-6000 rpm, and you may have a chance.  Of course, the car police should take the car away from him and give it to someone more deserving, but you get the idea....||||reg||1
Z||000007||loafer87gt||07-28-2001||01:54 PM||||Those S2000's aren't very forgiving to drive. What I mean is, you have to launch it just right to get a good launch. Down at the track a couple of monthts ago a guy brought a brand new s2000's, and after four launches his best ET was in the high 16's. He would either get horrible wheelspin off the line or bog it down. Maybe the guy was just a cack driver tho||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rogue_Ant||07-28-2001||02:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by loafer87gt:<BR><B>Those S2000's aren't very forgiving to drive. What I mean is, you have to launch it just right to get a good launch. Down at the track a couple of monthts ago a guy brought a brand new s2000's, and after four launches his best ET was in the high 16's. He would either get horrible wheelspin off the line or bog it down. Maybe the guy was just a cack driver tho</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well thats what you get for having only like 160ft-lbs of torque.  Lol they have so much horsepower, but no torque.  It must be kinda hard to launch it right.<P>Rogue<P>||||reg||1
